{
  "$note": [
    "Whole-block registration vectors. .NET BlockShape.From executes every declaration; the TS catalogue reader executes them too and grades none of the declaration rules but one.",
    "A true verdict means the descriptor/factory is admitted; a string is the refusal code.",
    "'declarations' are whole-block vectors graded by the declaration rules: ports are name -> DeclTerm, in order; 'subCanvases' maps a branch to its inputs and outputs.",
    "'expect' is true (admitted) or the refusal code, whose message must name the block ('name') and every entry of 'names'. 'expectPlugin' is the extra answer of .NET BlockShape.FromPlugin (a plugin's load); TypeScript has no plugin read and ignores it.",
    "'expectEditor' is the one refusal the TS catalogue reader makes: a declared term that does not parse under the declaration grammar. A vector without it is admitted by the reader, whatever 'expect' says: the server grades every other rule when it reads its catalogue.",
    "'expectDotnet': unrepresentable means the C# type of a port refuses the term before any declaration rule runs (PortTypeSyntaxException), so the vector is built in the editor half only.",
    "'hasDynamicPorts' (default false) is the block's flag.",
    "'secretValues' lists the names of the ports (of any position) that declare SecretValues; none by default."
  ],
